<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady in central markets.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady in central markets.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices remained steady in central Indian markets on Wednesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Arrivals were around 2,500 tonnes in central India, against 15,000 tonnes in the same period last year.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were also steady in very thin trade. The undertone remained steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices remained firm on good exports demand. Soymeal yellow was $293-294 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was $115-116 per tonne for ready shipment and was $114-115 per tonne for March-April shipment in export. Rapeseed extraction was 3,850-3,900 rupees per tonne for ready delivery and was 3,800 rupees per tonne for March-April delivery in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. The undertone was steady.</p>
